      "writtenOn": "2023-11-13T13:36:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "follow up question: If two devices can share the same `pviommu`, then should we treat \u0027multiple pviommus with the same id\u0027 as error? What about we just merging those pviommus?\n\nFor an example, let me assume following FDT.\n\n```\n/{\n  a { \u003ciommus\u003e \u003d \u003c\u0026pviommu_a\u003e; };\n  b { \u003ciommus\u003e \u003d \u003c\u0026pviommu_b\u003e; };\n  pviommu_a: pviommu_a { ... \u003cid\u003e\u003d\u003c0x1\u003e; .. };\n  pviommu_b: pviommu_b { ... \u003cid\u003e\u003d\u003c0x1\u003e; .. };\n}\n```\n\nInstead of considering it as error, what about treat it as warning and patch platform DT as follows?\n\n```\n/{\n  a { \u003ciommus\u003e \u003d \u003c\u0026pviommu_a\u003e; };\n  b { \u003ciommus\u003e \u003d \u003c\u0026pviommu_a\u003e; };  // pvmfw consider pviommu_a and pviommu_b as the same. so share one pviommu.\n  pviommu_a: pviommu_a { ... \u003cid\u003e\u003d\u003c0x1\u003e; .. };\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "bfe0c465_e099bec6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "5d139c8977760880bd085ba389ff95ec88f08576",
