      "writtenOn": "2023-11-15T13:01:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why did you make `DeviceAssignmentInfo::assigned_pviommus` a `BTreeMap` instead of a `BTreeSet`? this sounds like an unnecessary complication as the dictionary is now storing key-value pairs where the value is identical to the key and as we don\u0027t plan to add more pvIOMMU properties beyond their IDs.\n\nSimilarly, there\u0027s no need for the `PvIommu` type (`PvIommuId` suffices) and instead of lines 359-367, a `BTreeMap` `assigned_pviommus` can be trivially built from `pviommu_ids`:\n```\nlet mut assigned_pviommus \u003d BTreeSet::new();\nfor id in pviommu_ids.values() {\n    if !assigned_pviommus.insert(id) {\n        return Err(...);\n    }\n}\n```\nor, as you seem to like iterators:\n```\nlet all_ids_unique \u003d pviommu_ids.values().all(|id| assigned_pviommus.insert(id));\nif !all_ids_unique {\n    return Err(...);\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "a044a617_8008067f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 290,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 290,
        "endChar": 1
      },
