      "writtenOn": "2023-11-16T15:20:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d say having only one makes more sense (and, as I suggested above, deriving it from the phandle-to-ID map is trivial) but more importantly, your implementation currently removes any pvIOMMU that 1. doesn\u0027t have a `\u003cphandle\u003e` (I guess that\u0027s fine, to some extent) or 2. isn\u0027t attached to a device coming from the VM DTBO.\n\nIt isn\u0027t the role of pvmfw to \"clean-up\" the DT, only to sanitize it; if something is safe, we should allow it. Therefore, those unattached pvIOMMUs (which the uAPI permits creating, BTW) should be carried over and the `assigned_pviommus` actually are `iommu_ids` (but computing it outside of `parse_pviommus()` would be clearer, IMO).\n\nOn this point, I\u0027d recommend removing the comment on line 359.",
